  questionText: '5. The vertical position of an aircraft at or below the transition
    altitude will be reported as:'
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: At or below the transition altitude, aircraft use the local QNH
    pressure setting. Therefore, their vertical position is expressed as altitude
    above mean sea level rather than flight level.
  options:
  - Flight level
  - Whatever the Pilot Chooses
  - Altitude
  - Height
  correctOptionIndex: 2
